.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd October 10, 2026
.Dt SERVICE_RUNTIME 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm service_runtime
.Nd bounded provider runtime policies
.Sh LIBRARY
Service Library (libservice, -lservice)
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In service_runtime.h
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These helpers share provider policy without granting authority or owning the
provider lifecycle.
All value objects and lease sets require caller
serialization.
They may be embedded in provider-specific state.
.Pp
.Fn service_budget_begin milliseconds
starts a non-nestable thread-local monotonic budget for subsequent libservice
RPC waits, including bootstrap discovery, provider handshakes and calls.
Zero and UINT32_MAX are invalid.
A nested begin fails with EBUSY.
Call
.Fn service_budget_end
on every exit path.
Forked children do not inherit an active budget.
An exhausted budget fails with ETIMEDOUT before issuing another RPC.
Timeout does not undo an operation already delivered to its provider.
Budgets do not bound arbitrary callbacks, mutex contention, allocation,
scheduler delays, or kernel device operations.
.Pp
.Fn service_retry_init retry initial_ms maximum_ms
initializes immediate eligibility, with a nonzero initial delay and a maximum
at least as large.
Test eligibility with
.Fn service_retry_ready retry now_ms .
.Fn service_retry_result retry now_ms success
resets on success or doubles the failure delay up to the maximum.
Retries do not replay requests; callers must decide which operations are safe.
.Pp
.Fn service_health_record health error
updates saturating success, failure, consecutive-failure and transition
counters.
Initialize health to zero.
The return value reports a transition
between healthy and failed so a provider can log once per transition.
This is local accounting, not an externally published diagnostic protocol.
.Pp
.Fn service_drain_wait predicate argument timeout_ms
checks a nonblocking predicate against one absolute monotonic deadline.
The predicate returns 1 when complete, 0 when pending, or -1 with errno on
failure.
The helper sleeps at most ten milliseconds between checks and
returns ETIMEDOUT on expiry.
Signals do not restart the timeout.
The helper does not kill workers or cancel threads;
that remains provider policy.
.Pp
.Fn service_channels_wait kqueue_fd slots count listener_fd timeout_ms
services at most 256 borrowed channels, one bounded libchannel dispatch batch
per ready session.
It returns listener readiness (0 or 1), or -1 for a
kevent/listener error.
Per-channel errors are written to slot.error.
The caller retains channel ownership and must destroy failed sessions.
Use a dedicated kqueue and close channels before reusing slots.
Use listener_fd -1 to omit a listener.
Timeout -1 means unlimited.
Callbacks must not destroy channels or recursively enter this helper.
.Pp
.Fn service_lease_set_create capacity result
allocates a bounded set of at most 65536 entries.
.Fn service_lease_acquire set owner result
returns a nonzero token.
Owners must be nonzero provider-assigned session IDs.
.Fn service_lease_release set owner token
requires the matching owner; stale and foreign tokens both return ENOENT.
.Fn service_lease_release_owner set owner
reclaims all leases on session disconnect.
.Fn service_lease_count set
reports the current count.
Tokens never wrap or get reused within a set;
exhaustion returns EOVERFLOW.
Capacity exhaustion returns ENOSPC.
.Fn service_lease_set_destroy set
releases the set.
No helper authorizes a lease or survives provider restart.
.Ss Process teardown
.Fn service_processes_stop head
stops a caller-owned list of
.Vt struct service_process
nodes, each containing a
.Va next
pointer and a process descriptor in
.Va pd .
Nodes must be allocated with
.Xr malloc 3
or
.Xr calloc 3 .
The caller must be the parent, own each descriptor exclusively, and serialize
list access; the list must be acyclic and descriptors must not be duplicated.
.Pp
All children are signalled with SIGKILL before waiting for their exit.
Interrupted waits are retried.
Already-exited or already-reaped children are allowed.
In particular, ESRCH from pdwait indicates an already-reaped process
on this system; ECHILD is also tolerated.
Every node is freed, every descriptor is closed, and the head is cleared,
including on failure.
An empty list succeeds; a NULL head pointer fails with EINVAL.
The return value is 0 on success or -1 with the first error in errno.
After an error, remaining reap attempts are nonblocking; children whose
termination failed may still exist and require supervisor recovery.
.Pp
This function allocates no memory and grants no process authority.
It does not revoke descriptors previously delivered by a child.
It has no wait deadline and does not protect children against abrupt parent
death; callers must not advertise a bounded teardown time.
It does not acknowledge provider shutdown.
.Pp
.Fn service_bootstrap_parent fd timeout_ms
borrows an exclusively used local stream socket for a parent/child bootstrap.
It reads one native integer status, then sends byte 1 if the status is zero.
A positive status becomes errno; negative status fails with EPROTO and an
incomplete status at EOF fails with EIO.
Socket errors are preserved, SIGPIPE is suppressed, and EINTR and EAGAIN
retry under one monotonic deadline covering both status and acknowledgement.
Zero timeout, UINT32_MAX, and negative descriptors fail with EINVAL;
expiry fails with ETIMEDOUT.
The return value is 0 on success or -1 with errno on failure.
The socket flags are unchanged and the descriptor remains caller-owned on
both success and failure.
The protocol is local to processes sharing this ABI, not a network format.
Do not reuse a failed handshake stream: the peer may have observed partial
progress.
The caller must close or retain the socket according to its worker
lifecycle and terminate/reap failed children as necessary.
No authority is granted and no child cleanup or hard scheduling bound is
provided by this helper.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libservice 3 ,
.Xr BSDMemory 8 ,
.Xr BSDPower 8
